#{[17592186400597 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400597 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131485" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400597 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400597 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400597 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a5eae7d8-0877-5f8b-8a7a-fca7737eb497" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400597 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form. The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+7z=-3 \\\\ 0x+y-2z=2 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+7z=-3 \\\\ y-2z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-2z=2\\,⇒\\,y=2z+2\n$$\n\nand from the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\nx+7z=-3\\,⇒\\,x=-7z-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-7z-3 \\\\ y=2z+2 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7z-3 \\\\ 2z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400598 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400598 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400598 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400598 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400598 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400598 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400598 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400598 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186400600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400598 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bdb79457-f181-5b77-98a7-2247b1af411b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400599 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}7z+3 \\\\ 2z-2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400599 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400599 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee44784e-c13a-5b12-af97-8b32c8c0a5be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400600 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-7z-3 \\\\ 2z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400600 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400600 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "230fd32d-be4a-579c-925a-53e385a20db2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400601 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}7z-3 \\\\ 2-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400601 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400601 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c1affba9-f056-51a7-a549-36a67d2e8dca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400602 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-7z-3 \\\\ 2-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400602 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400602 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c81a8969-331d-5a2b-a2ad-56d7d447802b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400603 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}3-7z \\\\ 2z+2 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400603 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400603 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "74fab224-971f-5289-87ed-552b598c900e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400604 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400604 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400604 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400604 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400604 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a36d5833-a8f6-5e41-9f0c-9e264c1ac49c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400604 #edb/ref 1074 "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-8y+6z=-4 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x-8y+6z=-4\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=4y-3z-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4y-3z-2 \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$, $z$ (free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y-3z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186400605 #edb/r