070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402495 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x & \\text{ for }\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<0 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & \\text{ for }\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x<\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402495 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "65911f9a-fa00-54b8-9673-9586456d002e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402495 #edb/ref 1074 "The right-sided limit ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)$ does not exist since $f(x)$ is not defined on the interval $x\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ \n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nApproaching $x=0$ from the left, we have $x<0,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)=\\text{DNE},\\,{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402496 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402496 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402496 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186402499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402496 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9766008d-bd13-5a70-b8fc-147a47588ba7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402497 #edb/ref 1080 "{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x)=0,\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x)=1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402497 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 1759