#edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402753 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a16d7da4-393e-5805-87b6-3a9b82bafe2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402754 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402754 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402754 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "123f0263-f92c-574c-8223-205921ca12c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402755 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402755 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402755 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5842cb4f-dfe1-5bcd-a5d1-aca7e442c719" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42019" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y+2z=2 \\\\  & y-z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "013e11bb-39c0-595b-a244-03847638286f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402756 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=0 \\\\  & y-z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ y=z-1 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186402761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402757 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0fa49e40-cb09-52a9-be51-216ec3f67938" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402758 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402758 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402758 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e80e6ba-d53c-56a1-8f14-814656e252d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402759 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402759 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402759 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "240d49db-221f-5c96-a2c7-752016dd8d06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402760 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-z \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402760 #edb/ref 1082